1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,783
Your AI feature needs

2
00:00:01,783 --> 00:00:03,249
acceptance criteria too.

3
00:00:03,249 --> 00:00:04,532
They're called evals.

4
00:00:05,632 --> 00:00:06,615
An eval has three

5
00:00:06,615 --> 00:00:06,962
parts.

6
00:00:06,962 --> 00:00:08,119
Real example inputs.

7
00:00:08,119 --> 00:00:09,391
Written criteria for a

8
00:00:09,391 --> 00:00:10,085
good answer.

9
00:00:10,085 --> 00:00:10,836
And a grader:

10
00:00:10,836 --> 00:00:11,126
code,

11
00:00:11,126 --> 00:00:11,646
a person,

12
00:00:11,646 --> 00:00:12,629
or another model.

13
00:00:13,729 --> 00:00:14,980
Ask the same question

14
00:00:14,980 --> 00:00:15,338
twice,

15
00:00:15,338 --> 00:00:16,410
and the answer can

16
00:00:16,410 --> 00:00:16,827
change.

17
00:00:16,827 --> 00:00:17,781
So one good demo

18
00:00:17,781 --> 00:00:18,913
proves very little.

19
00:00:20,013 --> 00:00:21,881
Start with real conversations.

20
00:00:21,881 --> 00:00:23,002
Mark each one pass

21
00:00:23,002 --> 00:00:23,500
or fail,

22
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:24,621
with one line why.

23
00:00:25,721 --> 00:00:26,268
This week,

24
00:00:26,268 --> 00:00:27,579
take twenty real inputs,

25
00:00:27,579 --> 00:00:28,126
mark them,

26
00:00:28,126 --> 00:00:29,219
and group the fails.

27
00:00:29,219 --> 00:00:30,312
The biggest group is

28
00:00:30,312 --> 00:00:31,460
your first criterion.

29
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:33,627
Write down what good

30
00:00:33,627 --> 00:00:34,213
looks like,

31
00:00:34,213 --> 00:00:35,280
before you judge the

32
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:35,653
output.

